34. Key DBA Point
The most important thing to demonstrate to the ISCP team is that AWS failover is only one part of disaster recovery.
Your DBA process is:
Baseline → Detect → Assess → Notify → Failover → Monitor → Oracle Validation → Application Validation → GoldenGate/DMS Validation → Security Review → Backup Review → RTO Measurement → Documentation → Closure
That is the story you want the auditors/ISCP team to see.
AWS states that traditional Multi-AZ failovers typically take 60–120 seconds, but the actual time varies with database activity and recovery conditions. Also, after failover, DNS propagation and client reconnection can add additional recovery time. Therefore, your business RTO should be based on your measured end-to-end recovery, not simply the RDS failover duration.
